{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life","id":1529233,"title":"The Roman Kindred during Julius Caesar life?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-23T11:02:26-08:00","id":1529233,"title":"The Roman Kindred during Julius Caesar life?","content":"Hi guys, I just watched a video about Julius Caesar by Overly Sarcastic Productions, and I thought it'd be fun to ask. Do we know what the Vampire populatiom of Rome was during his life, which clams were present in Rome, what roads they followed and everything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T11:04:54-08:00","id":1529235,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of. But I played in a game once where Julius Caesar was the favored mortal protege of a Ventrue elder named Marius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T11:15:56-08:00","id":1529236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529235#post1529235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I know of. But I played in a game once where Julius Caesar was the favored mortal protege of a Ventrue elder named Marius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rome was canonically Clan Ventrue's baby,right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T12:05:06-08:00","id":1529237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529236#post1529236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rome was canonically Clan Ventrue's baby,right?</div> </div> </div> </div>So do the Ventrue claim and no Camarilla Clan has really tried to contest that, but how many kindred of the period around to confirm such assertion have we been presented with?<br /> As with everything involving kindred, facts should be taken with a grain of salt, as the memoirs are written by the last one standing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T12:26:30-08:00","id":1529238,"title":"","content":"The clanbooks go into it with their own bias included. Ventrue came with the Etruscans around 800BC, Tinia ruled first then Camilla so the Ventrue claim is pretty reasonable, they were there from the beginning. Toreader had been around since the Greek colonies so they flocked to Rome when it started getting important. Camilla valued the Malkavians' advice so he went to Tryphosa, she had visions of bad stuff if he didn't destroy Carthage so the Malks also scrambled to join his side<br /> <br /> Those three were the main clans of Rome until the Punic Wars when Camilla called for an alliance of clans, the Lasombra came en masse first, then the Cappadocians, then smatterings of the rest of the clans or so the Ventrue say. It was pretty cosmopolitan after that but those first three clans were always the most important<br /> <br /> No clue what roads they preferred back then\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T13:23:06-08:00","id":1529239,"title":"","content":"Rome was the kingdom of the Lasombra, Malkavian and Ventrue clans in all the lore that has been submitted so far. Or at the very least had the strongest influence over the city, but many clans like the Toreador, Nosferatu and the Followers of Set had a strong presence that shouldn't be discounted. As for roads I can see Roads Of Kings, Heaven and Humanity being the most popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-23-2024, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T13:44:16-08:00","id":1529245,"title":"","content":"The only clans that I can't seeing having much of a presence in Rome would be Ravnos, Tzismce, Banu Haqim or the Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T14:20:43-08:00","id":1529248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529245#post1529245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only clans that I can't seeing having much of a presence in Rome would be Ravnos, Tzismce, Banu Haqim or the Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Brujah are probably...elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Across the pond if you will.<br /> <br /> Alongside the Salubri AKA the Baali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T14:29:25-08:00","id":1529250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529248#post1529248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Brujah are probably...elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Across the pond if you will.<br /> <br /> Alongside the Salubri AKA the Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if there's elephants there \ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T14:36:18-08:00","id":1529251,"title":"","content":"We had<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game#post1494196\"> a thread along similar lines</a> a while back. <br /> <br /> Most Roman Kindred at the end of the Roman Republic are going to associate the Ravnos with the Egyptian Alexandrian jati of diplomats, merchants, and sailors, and the city of Rome at that time drew merchants from at least as far as India and Ethiopia. <br /> <br /> Also, for anyone who has never seen the two-season tv series <b>Rome</b> that HBO did about 20 years ago, I highly recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T15:08:49-08:00","id":1529252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529250#post1529250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if there's elephants there \ud83d\ude02</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that the Baali's extinguishment as a Bloodline starts from Carthage and basically continues until it's MOSTLY DONE by the Inquisition. The only survivors being Mary the Black and the ones in torpor or who fled to the New World.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim's work against the Baali pretty much helped define their view of European Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T01:13:19-08:00","id":1529290,"title":"","content":"Camilla is on the Road of Sin thanks to the influence of a Brujah lover who went there after Carthage's destruction.<br /> At some point, each clan got a part of Rome nominally assigned to them, but not every clan claimed the place. Ex.: Banu Haqim never bothered establishing a presence in the area assigned to them.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu were probably there from the beginning or soon after because they're crucial to the Cainite infrastructure that revolves around the city's catacombs.<br /> <br /> At some point the vampiric senate decided to become the \u0130nconnu.<br /> <br /> There are more details on Rome's vampiric history in VDA20's Companion and also on the fandom wiki, based on material scattered across multiple manuals.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget that in Carthage there were also some Assamites allied with the Brujah. \u0130f the Brujah were indeed maneuvered by the Baali, \u0130'd say those Assamites were too.<br /> <br /> Lasombra had an important presence in \u0130taly, considering that their Antediluvian was based in Sicily and active in ancient times (Set and [Lasombra] are probably the latest active antediluvians in recorded history), though they were second to the Ventrue in Rome, based on who the prince was.<br /> <br /> As it has already been said, after the destruction of Carthage and Rome's growth in importance, most clans came to the city (and had a portion of it assigned to them, as \u0130 said), though the most important clans seemed to have remained the Ventrue, the Malkavians and the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Notice also that VDA20's introduction of Warriors of Glycon and Witches of Echidna should see them present during the Roman Empire: the witches are said to have been famous oracles and priests respected and sought out by the other clans in antiquity, until the Followers of Set ruined the clan's image. Glycon was a popular deity in the late Roman Empire, attracting even the devotion of emperor Marcus Aurelius, therefore Warriors of Glycon (who are also the Setite clan's ruler and leaders until they are purged after 1244) should justifiably be portrayed as influential in the empire, even if not necessarily massive in Rome itself.<br /> Unfortunately both bloodlines have very limited wordcount in the manuals and not enough has been written to explain how the metaplot and vampire history (including clan histor) was affected by them. But, as \u0130 said, witches are said to have been important in antiquity, and the warriors' importance can be inferred from their connection to Glycon and rulership over the clan.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T01:19:49-08:00","id":1529292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529252#post1529252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think that the Baali's extinguishment as a Bloodline starts from Carthage and basically continues until it's MOSTLY DONE by the Inquisition. The only survivors being Mary the Black and the ones in torpor or who fled to the New World.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim's work against the Baali pretty much helped define their view of European Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Baali Wars were in prehistoric times (second city, if memory serves me well) and in the early middle ages on Crete. To my memory, Carthage was not Baali, but Baali-influenced because of Moloch's influence over the Carthaginian Brujahs. But Roman vampires did not actually fight the Baali in Carthage, but the Brujah and Banu Haqim. The Baali bloodline was never exitinguished. It was simply in hiding since the antediluvians allegedly got together to destroy them at the time of the Second City, and they existed in hiding since, only resurfacing in a noticeable way during the Baali War in Crete.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T06:47:18-08:00","id":1529300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529292#post1529292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Baali Wars were in prehistoric times (second city, if memory serves me well) and in the early middle ages on Crete. To my memory, Carthage was not Baali, but Baali-influenced because of Moloch's influence over the Carthaginian Brujahs. But Roman vampires did not actually fight the Baali in Carthage, but the Brujah and Banu Haqim. The Baali bloodline was never exitinguished. It was simply in hiding since the antediluvians allegedly got together to destroy them at the time of the Second City, and they existed in hiding since, only resurfacing in a noticeable way during the Baali War in Crete.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah....and the Baali are DONE by the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> So the question of when that happens is an important one. Seeing Moloch underneath Carthage with Troile seems a pretty good time for them to suffer an irreversible blow to their power base that they've never recovered from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T10:23:02-08:00","id":1529314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529300#post1529300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah....and the Baali are DONE by the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> So the question of when that happens is an important one. Seeing Moloch underneath Carthage with Troile seems a pretty good time for them to suffer an irreversible blow to their power base that they've never recovered from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are DONE at all. They've always been hiding. They still exist in Masquerade. Moloch himself is stirring under Carthage's rubble (or something is and people are making sacrifices to Moloch). Other elders are in South America. Infernalism is a recurrent infection in the Sabbat and they are likely involved. A faction of them plots and acts from withing the Tal'Mahe'Ra. I'm not sure whether they have any canon involvement with the Inconnu (some demon does, at least, considering Hunedoara castle) but they might as well, it would make sense. Ur Shulgi could totally be serving their interests. Tryphosa's infant is researching into the ancient Malkavian ordos and one of the three was an infernalist one, so Baali can totally reappear from there too.<br /> <br /> They were considered extinct after the first Baali war in the First or Second City (depending on accounts) and resurfaced a VERY long time after. Whenever they appeared, they seem to have taken vampiric society by surprise. I see no canon metaplot reason to say they are done, though I admit I'm not a Baali expert. They're doing the same thing they've been doing since the first Baali war: plot in hiding and make the world forget about them.<br /> <br /> By some accounts, both Mariah the Black's stuff and the mess in Cnossos with the Assamites occur well after Carthage.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Saulot and Tzimisce are both on the list of suspected founders (though I prefer considering these as Tremere lies) and both are active in some way in Gehenna especially through Tremere. Ur Shulgi is also (strangely) on the list and he's active. The Unnamed is still unidentified and possibly active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T11:05:39-08:00","id":1529319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529233-the-roman-kindred-during-julius-caesar-life?p=1529314#post1529314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think they are DONE at all. They've always been hiding. They still exist in Masquerade. Moloch himself is stirring under Carthage's rubble (or something is and people are making sacrifices to Moloch). Other elders are in South America. Infernalism is a recurrent infection in the Sabbat and they are likely involved. A faction of them plots and acts from withing the Tal'Mahe'Ra. I'm not sure whether they have any canon involvement with the Inconnu (some demon does, at least, considering Hunedoara castle) but they might as well, it would make sense. Ur Shulgi could totally be serving their interests. Tryphosa's infant is researching into the ancient Malkavian ordos and one of the three was an infernalist one, so Baali can totally reappear from there too.<br /> <br /> They were considered extinct after the first Baali war in the First or Second City (depending on accounts) and resurfaced a VERY long time after. Whenever they appeared, they seem to have taken vampiric society by surprise. I see no canon metaplot reason to say they are done, though I admit I'm not a Baali expert. They're doing the same thing they've been doing since the first Baali war: plot in hiding and make the world forget about them.<br /> <br /> By some accounts, both Mariah the Black's stuff and the mess in Cnossos with the Assamites occur well after Carthage.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Saulot and Tzimisce are both on the list of suspected founders (though I prefer considering these as Tremere lies) and both are active in some way in Gehenna especially through Tremere. Ur Shulgi is also (strangely) on the list and he's active. The Unnamed is still unidentified and possibly active.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more interesting to have them be crushed and scattered like the Salubri<br /> <br /> V:TM doesn't need EVIL Demon Worshipers to be their villains.<br /> <br /> YMMV.<br /> <br /> But yes, in my campaigns, Carthage is when the Baali ceased to matter as an interesting historical detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the 